==Pros & Cons==

=== Pros: ===
*High damage and DPS.
*High damage and DPS at a low level.
*High range at low level.
*Good range.
*Has AoE. (Every 10 normal kicks) 
*High AoE damage
*Good for endless mode due to AoE attack
*A small hitbox (you can put a lot in one place)
=== Cons: ===
*Very expensive to upgrade, Having the same Last Level Total Cost as [[Mech Bunny Titan]].
*Expensive to place without farm units. 
*It is a P2W unit.
*Can't block stuns.

==Strategy==
Place them near unstunning units like [[Camera Repair Drone]], [[Speaker Repair Drone]], Medic Cameraman, and Streamer Cameraman or unstunnable units like [[Leprechaun Cameraman]], [[Shield Cameraman]], and [[Healer TV Woman|Healer Tv Woman]].

Place them near each other so they can deal the maximum amount of damage, and place them away from the track so it is  harder for Toilets to stun them.

In [[Endless Mode]], use a loadout of any [[Farms]] or [[Printers|Printer Units]] (recommended [[Large Printer Man]], [[Titan Printer Man]] or [[Santa TV Man]]), [[Titan Fanman]], [[Astro Upgraded Titan Cameraman]] (or any good slowing unit) and boosters like [[DJ TV Man]] or [[Clockwoman]] and [[Leprechaun Cameraman]].

==Trivia==

* One of the few good units that can be placed in the magnification radius of [[Titan Mogman]].
* It emits small white sparks around itself(But it could just be for visual effects).
* In the description of the update when it was added, it said "This unit doesn't like toilets!".

